  "solution": {
    "text": "For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> (from the graph).In this situation, the circuit can be drawn as shown in figure <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> .<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0053_f2ba717433f3.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" /><br /><br />[current through R<sub>2&nbsp;</sub>will be zero because we have a short circuit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>]<br /><br />Here <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>36</mn><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math><br /><br />or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> ...(1)<br /><br />current will not flow through <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>R</mi> <mn>3</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math>, it will be open circuit.<br /><br />In this situation, the circuit can be drawn as shown figure <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> .<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0095_f3c8e37bffe4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 223px; height: 268px;\" /><br />Figure (B)<br /><br />Now <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>36</mn><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2&#160;</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;(given)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> ...(2)<br /><br />from Eqs. (1) and (2)<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>"
  }
